# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data. The raw dump is ~21 GB and the processed store is ~350 MB - neither
# belongs in git. Everything under data/ is rebuildable with `make ingest`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/**
!data/**/
!data/**/.gitkeep
!data/README.md
*.npy
*.npz
*.parquet
*.feather
Dataverse/
*.txt.gz

# Experiment artefacts: keep the config, metrics and run log, not the weights/predictions.
# The `!experiments/runs/**/` line is load-bearing: git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded, so without it the negations below never take effect
# and every run's evidence is silently dropped.
experiments/runs/**
!experiments/runs/**/
!experiments/runs/.gitkeep
!experiments/runs/**/config.yaml
!experiments/runs/**/metrics.json
!experiments/runs/**/run.log

# Two predictions arrays are the exception, and only two. Every result table and figure in
# the report is derived from a stored forecast: make_results.py and make_significance.py
# read EXP-008 (the reported run, 217 856 bytes) and make_period_breakdown.py additionally
# reads EXP-007 (the calendar-off control, 12 224 bytes). A clean clone cannot regenerate
# them under those ids, because run_experiment.py allocates the next free id rather than
# overwriting a finished run, so without these two files the documented reproduction chain
# cannot rebuild the exact evidence the report cites. Every other run's predictions stay
# untracked: they are inputs to no documented command, and 16 more arrays is bulk without
# a reader. These two negations must sit after `*.npy` (above) as well as after
# `experiments/runs/**`, since the last matching pattern decides.
!experiments/runs/EXP-008/predictions.npy
!experiments/runs/EXP-007/predictions.npy
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working material, not assignment deliverables: the transcribed brief and
# rubric, the work plan, the report outline, the video script and the drafting
# notes. These live in the workspace directory above this repository, so git
# does not normally see them. The rules below guard against a stray copy being
# added back in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLAUDE.md
project-docs/
docs/ASSIGNMENT.md
docs/RUBRIC.md
docs/PLAN.md
docs/REPORT_OUTLINE.md
docs/VIDEO_SCRIPT.md
docs/notes/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# Tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Report build artefacts (keep the final PDF, drop LaTeX intermediates).
# Anchored to reports/: unanchored *.log and *.out match at any depth and would swallow
# the per-run training logs the experiment trail depends on.
reports/*.aux
reports/*.log
reports/*.out
reports/*.synctex.gz
reports/*.bbl
reports/*.blg
reports/*.fls
reports/*.fdb_latexmk
